.TH KACHA 1 "2026-11-03" "kacha 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kacha \- capture the screen on Linux and macOS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kacha
[\fBregion\fR|\fBfull\fR|\fBarea \fIX,Y,WxH\fR|\fBversion\fR]
[\fIflags\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kacha
captures the screen, lets the user drag a part of it, annotates what they
picked, and copies the result to the clipboard and to the disk.
.PP
It captures Wayland sessions through \fForg.freedesktop.portal.Screenshot\fR,
and macOS through \fBscreencapture\fR. X11 is not supported.
.PP
On Wayland it copies through \fBwl-copy\fR when wl-clipboard is installed:
that leaves a process of its own serving the selection, so a capture stays
pasteable after \fBkacha\fR exits. Without it the capture goes through GTK,
and a desktop with no clipboard manager, as COSMIC, empties the clipboard
when the copying process ends.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B region
Capture the screen, show the captured frame full screen, and take the part
the user drags. What was picked then shows in the editor, with a toolbar
under it. Enter or a double click finishes, Escape or a right click cancels.
This is the default.
.TP
.B full
Capture the display under the pointer without a selection window.
.TP
.BI area " X,Y,WxH"
Capture a rectangle of the display under the pointer, in device independent
pixels from its top left corner.
.TP
.B permission
Ask the system for what a capture needs. On macOS that is the screen
recording permission of this copy, which shows its dialog once.
.TP
.B version
Print the version.
.SH EDITOR
The toolbar holds nine tools: rectangle, ellipse, arrow, pen, text, number,
emoji, mosaic and crop; five colors; three stroke widths; undo and redo; and
three buttons that end the capture: cancel, save to a file, and copy to the
clipboard.
.PP
A text is typed with the system's input method and settled with Enter or a
press elsewhere; the field it is typed in shows the capture through, so that
the text lands where it is meant to. A text already drawn is picked by a
click, and the drag that follows moves it; a double click opens it again, and
Escape leaves it as it was. A number is placed with a click, and counts on
from the numbers before it. An emoji comes from the panel the emoji tool opens,
which a second press of its button puts away, and lands in the middle of the
selection, picked: a drag moves it, and a drag of a corner resizes it. A drag
with the mosaic paints along the pointer with a brush wider than a stroke, and
one that holds Shift covers the box it spans: a band follows the brush and a
frame rounds the box as it is dragged, so that what the squares cover shows. A drag with the crop keeps the
part of the capture it covers, and drops the rest, the shapes moving with it.
Dragging a corner or a side of the selection resizes what is kept as well.
.TP
.B Enter
Keep the capture and copy it to the clipboard, as a double click does.
.TP
.B "Cmd+Z, Cmd+Shift+Z"
Undo and redo a shape. Cmd is Command on macOS and Control elsewhere.
.TP
.B Escape
Leave without a capture.
.SH FLAGS
.TP
.BI \-o ", " \-\-out " PATH"
Write the capture at PATH, which names a file or a directory, and turn
saving on. Defaults to \fB$KACHA_DIR\fR, else
\fB~/Pictures/Screenshots\fR, and names the file after the moment of the
capture.
.TP
.B \-\-stdout
Write the PNG to standard output instead of saving and copying; only the
\fBfull\fR command takes it.
.TP
.BI \-\-copy= BOOL
Copy the capture to the clipboard. True by default: a capture goes to the
clipboard unless a flag or a button asks for a file.
.TP
.BI \-\-save= BOOL
Write the capture to the disk. False by default, and on when \fB\-\-out\fR
names where to write.
.TP
.BI \-\-delay " D"
Wait D, as 1.5s, before capturing.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B KACHA_DIR
Where captures go unless \fB\-\-out\fR says otherwise.
.TP
.B KACHA_SOURCE
Take the capture from a PNG file instead of the screen, to try the selection
window where nothing can be captured.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
A capture was taken and delivered.
.TP
.B 1
An error, printed to standard error.
.TP
.B 130
The user canceled the selection.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
# A keybinding, here in a wlroots compositor's configuration
bindsym $mod+Shift+s exec kacha
# Save a fixed rectangle, no window, no clipboard
kacha area 0,0,1920x1080 --copy=false -o ~/tmp/
# Straight into a pipe
kacha full --stdout > shot.png
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR screencapture (1)
